      "worked": "Since $|4x-x^2|=|x|\\,|4-x|$, $x=0$ satisfies the inequality.\n\nFor $x\\ne0$, divide by the positive number $|x|$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}|4-x|&\\ge1\\\\4-x&\\ge1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad4-x\\le-1\\\\x&\\le3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x\\ge5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe case $x=0$ is already included, so $x\\le3$ or $x\\ge5$.",
